[356.0498, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 557 \u001b[22m       <h2>Questions, answered.</h2>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 558 \u001b[22m     </div>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 559 \u001b[22m     <div \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"faq reveal\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[8C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m0\u001b[18G\u001b[38;5;231m<details open><summary>How does Tidel\u001b[56Gne avoid\u001b[65Gfalse alarms?<spa\u001b[83G class=\"pm\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B>+</span></summa\u001b[29Gy><p>When a check fails, we re-run it right away fr\u001b[81Gm at least th\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bree othe\u001b[21G regions. You're\u001b[38Galerted\u001b[46Gonly\u001b[51Gif\u001b[54Ga\u001b[56Gmajority\u001b[65Gof\u001b[68Gthem\u001b[73Gagree\u001b[79Gthe\u001b[83Gservice\u001b[91Gis\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;231mdown,\u001b[18Gso\u001b[21Gone flaky\u001b[31Gnetwork pat\u001b[43G won't wake you.</p></details>\u001b[74G           \u001b[86G        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 560 +\u001b[38;5;231m      <details \u001b[38;5;148mopen\u001b[38;5;231m><summary>How does Tideline avoid false alarms?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m     +\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary><p>\u001b[48;5;28mEvery\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mmonitor\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mis\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mchecked\u001b[48;5;22m from \u001b[48;5;28m6\u001b[48;5;22m regions. You're alerted only\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m     +\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[48;5;28mwhen\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mat\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mleast\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28m2 \u001b[48;5;22mof them agree the service is down, so one flaky network path won'\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m     +\u001b[38;5;231mt wake you.</p></details>                                                         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 561 \u001b[22m       <details><summary>Do you charge per user?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary>\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m <p>No. Every paid plan includes unlimited teammates. Pricing is based on how many \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m monitors you run and how often they check.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 562 \u001b[22m       <details><summary>Can I migrate from my current tool?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</spa\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m n></summary><p>Yes. Import monitors from a CSV or from most popular uptime tools' \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m export formats. Most teams finish migrating in less than ten minutes.</p></details\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22m>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m63\u001b[14G\u001b[22m    <details><summary>What happens when I hit my monitor limit?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22m+</span></summary><p>Your existing monitors keep running. We'll ask you to upgrade\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m  or archive a monitor before you add another. We never switch off monitoring witho\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m ut warning.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[357.0136, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m9\u001b[16G\u001b[22m<div \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"faq reveal\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 560 -\u001b[38;5;231m      <details open><summary>How does Tideline avoid false alarms?<span class=\"pm\"\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m     -\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary><p>When a check fails, we re-run it right away from at least th\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;231mree\u001b[16Gother regions. You're alerted \u001b[47Gnly \u001b[52Gf a majority\u001b[65Gof them \u001b[74Ggree the service is \r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bdown, so one fl\u001b[28Gk\u001b[30G network\u001b[39Gpat\u001b[43G won't wake you.</p></details>    \u001b[78G    \u001b[83G  \u001b[86G     \u001b[92G  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 560 +\u001b[38;5;231m      <details \u001b[38;5;148mopen\u001b[38;5;231m><summary>How does Tideline avoid false alarms?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m     +\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary><p>\u001b[48;5;28mEvery\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mmonitor\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mis\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mchecked\u001b[48;5;22m from \u001b[48;5;28m6\u001b[48;5;22m regions. You're alerted only\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m   \u001b[13G\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[48;5;28mwhen\u001b[18Gat\u001b[48;5;22m \u001b[48;5;28mleast\u001b[27G2 \u001b[48;5;22mof them agree the service is down, so one flaky network path won'\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bt wake you.</p></details>  \u001b[40G       \u001b[48G  \u001b[51G       \u001b[59G    \u001b[64G \u001b[66G        \u001b[75G      \u001b[82G       \u001b[90G    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 561 \u001b[22m       <details><summary>Do you charge per user?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary>\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m <p>No. Every paid plan includes unlimited teammates. Pricing is based on how many \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22mmonitors you run and how \u001b[38Gften\u001b[43Gt\u001b[45Gey check.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m562\u001b[12G\u001b[22m      <details><summ\u001b[33Gry>Can I migrate from my current tool?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</spa\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bn></summary><p>Yes. Import mo\u001b[42Gi\u001b[44Gors\u001b[48Gfrom a CSV or from most popular uptime tools' \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22mexport format\u001b[26G. Most teams finish migrating in less \u001b[65Ghan ten mi\u001b[76Gutes.</p></details\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m563\u001b[12G\u001b[22m      <detail\u001b[26G><summary>What happens when I\u001b[56Ghit my monitor li\u001b[75Gt?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B+</span></summary><p>Your existing monitors keep running. We'll ask you to upgrade\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[13G\u001b[22mor\u001b[16Garchive a monitor before\u001b[41Gyou add\u001b[49Ganother. We never switch off monitoring witho\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1But war\u001b[19Ging.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(index.html)\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[357.0282, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[21B\u001b[38;5;246m \r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;174m*\u001b[9G\u001b[38;5;216mng\u2026\u001b[18G\u001b[38;5;246m2\u001b[28G6\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[357.0532, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[9G\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m8\u001b[17G\u001b[22m/div>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 559 \u001b[22m     <div \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"faq reveal\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 560 \u001b[22m       <details \u001b[38;5;148mopen\u001b[38;5;231m><summary>How does Tideline avoid false alarms?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m >+</span></summary><p>Every monitor is checked from 6 regions. You're alerted only\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m  when at least 2 of them agree the service is down, so one flaky network path won'\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m t wake you.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 561 -\u001b[38;5;231m      <details><summary>Do you charge per user?<span class=\"pm\">+</span></summary>\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m     -\u001b[38;5;231m<p>No. Every paid plan includes unlimited teammates. Pricing is based on how many \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m     -\u001b[38;5;231mmonitors you run and how often they check.</p></details>                          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 561 +\u001b[38;5;231m      <details><summary>Do you charge per user?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary>\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m     +\u001b[38;5;231m<p>No. Pricing is based on how many monitors you run.</p></details>               \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m562\u001b[12G\u001b[22m      <details><summary>Can I migrate from my current tool?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</spa\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22mn></summary><p\u001b[27GYes. Import monito\u001b[46Gs from a\u001b[55GCSV o\u001b[61G from m\u001b[69Gst popular uptime tool\u001b[92G' \r\u001b[11C\u001b[1Bexport fo\u001b[22Gmats. Most teams\u001b[39Gfi\u001b[43Gsh mig\u001b[50Gating in\u001b[59Gless than ten minutes.</p></details\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m563\u001b[12G\u001b[22m      <details><summary>What happens when I hit my monitor limit?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22m+</span></summary><p>Your existing monitors\u001b[56Gkeep running. We'll ask you to upgrade\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B or archive a monitor before you add another. We\u001b[61Gnever switch off monitoring witho\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1But w\u001b[18Gning.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m564\u001b[12G\u001b[22m  \u001b[15G   <details\u001b[28Gsumm\u001b[33Gry>Is there an API?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summary><p>Yes.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m  There's a full REST API, a CLI, and a Terraform provider. Anything you can do in \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m the dashboard, you can also script.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
