 \u001b[66G          \u001b[77G                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 563 \u001b[22m       <details><summary>What happens when I hit my monitor limit?<span \u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m +</span></summary><p>Your existing monitors keep running. We'll ask you to upgrade\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[13G\u001b[22mor\u001b[16Garchive a monitor before\u001b[41Gyou add\u001b[49Ganother. We never switch off monitoring witho\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1But war\u001b[19Ging.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m564\u001b[13G\u001b[22m  \u001b[16G  <details><summary>Is there\u001b[46Gn API?<span\u001b[58G\u001b[38;5;148mclass\u001b[38;5;231m=\u001b[38;5;186m\"pm\"\u001b[38;5;231m>+</span></summa\u001b[85Gy><p>Yes.\r\u001b[11C\u001b[1B There's a full REST API, a CLI, and a Terraform provider. Anything you can do in \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m   \u001b[12G\u001b[22mthe\u001b[16Gdashbo\u001b[23Grd, yo\u001b[30G c\u001b[33Gn al\u001b[38Go sc\u001b[43Gipt.</p></details>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m565\u001b[13G\u001b[22m   </div>\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(index.html)\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
